{"id":"u2","lessons":[{"id":"u2-l1","title":"名词与冠词","subtitle":"英语的基石与迷宫——从可数性到 a/an/the/零冠词","intro":[{"title":"为什么冠词让中国人头疼？","body":"汉语里说「一只狗」「那只狗」「狗很可爱」，用的是独立的词「一只」「那只」或干脆不说。英语却把这些意思压缩进 **a / an / the / 零冠词**，内嵌在名词前，而且规则远不止「定/不定」这么简单。\n\n好消息是：冠词的选择有规律可循。本关从名词分类出发，一步步拆解冠词的所有核心用法，让你告别凭感觉猜测。"},{"title":"名词分类——可数 vs. 不可数","body":"英语名词最核心的区分是**可数（Countable）与不可数（Uncountable）**，因为这直接决定能用什么冠词。\n\n| 类别 | 特征 | 例词 |\n|------|------|------|\n| 可数名词 | 有单/复数，可用 a/an | book, idea, chair |\n| 不可数名词 | 无复数，不用 a/an | water, music, advice |\n\n**不可数名词六大类型：**\n1. 液体/气体：water, milk, air\n2. 材料/物质：wood, iron, paper（纸）\n3. 抽象概念：love, freedom, knowledge\n4. 学科/领域：mathematics, music\n5. 活动/运动：swimming, chess\n6. 集合概念：furniture, luggage, equipment","tip":"paper（纸，不可数）vs. a paper（一篇论文/一份报纸，可数）——同一个词在不同语境可数性会变化！"},{"title":"语境改变可数性的典型例子","body":"很多名词在不同语境下会在可数和不可数之间切换：\n\n- **coffee（咖啡）**：I drink coffee every morning.（不可数）→ Two coffees, please.（两杯咖啡，可数）\n- **hair（头发）**：She has beautiful hair.（不可数）→ There's a hair in my soup!（一根头发，可数）\n- **room（空间/房间）**：We need more room.（空间，不可数）→ The hotel has 200 rooms.（可数）\n- **life（生命/生活）**：Life is short.（抽象不可数）→ She led an interesting life.（一种生活方式，可数）","tip":"遇到陌生名词，不要只记单词，要连同「可数/不可数」一起记忆！"},{"title":"a vs. an——看发音，不看拼写","body":"选 a 还是 an，规则只有一条：**看后面单词的第一个音素**，是元音音素用 an，是辅音音素用 a。\n\n**用 an 的情况（以元音音素开头）：**\n- an apple /æpl/（a 发 /æ/）\n- an hour /aʊər/（h 不发音，以 /aʊ/ 开头）\n- an MBA（M 发 /em/，以元音音素开头）\n- an X-ray（X 发 /eks/）\n\n**用 a 的情况（以辅音音素开头）：**\n- a university（u 发 /juː/，以辅音 /j/ 开头！）\n- a European（e 发 /j/）\n- a one-way street（one 发 /wʌn/，以 /w/ 开头）","tip":"「an honest man」中 h 不发音；「a university」中 u 发 /juː/。永远看发音，不看字母！"},{"title":"不定冠词 a/an 的五大功能","body":"**功能1：首次提及，泛指单数可数名词**\n- I saw **a** dog in the park.（第一次提到这只狗）\n\n**功能2：表示数量「一个」**\n- Wait **a** moment. / I'll be back in **an** hour.\n\n**功能3：泛指整个类别**\n- **A** whale is a mammal.（鲸鱼是哺乳动物）\n\n**功能4：表示职业/身份**\n- She is **a** doctor. / He became **a** Buddhist.\n\n**功能5：感叹句 What a/an...!**\n- What **a** beautiful day! / What **an** interesting idea!"},{"title":"定冠词 the——已知、唯一、特指","body":"the 的核心逻辑：**说话双方都知道在说哪个**。主要场景：\n\n**已知信息：**\n- I saw a dog. **The** dog was barking loudly.（第二次提起，换用 the）\n- Please close **the** door.（房间里只有一扇门）\n\n**世界唯一：**\n- **the** sun, **the** moon, **the** earth, **the** sky\n\n**最高级/序数词前：**\n- **the** tallest building / **the** first chapter\n\n**特殊用法：**\n- She plays **the** piano.（演奏乐器，球类/棋类不加）\n- **the** poor / **the** rich（the + 形容词 = 一类人）\n- in **the** morning / on **the** whole（固定短语）","tip":"地理名称规律：加 the 的有河流(the Thames)、海洋、山脉(the Alps)、含 Republic/States/Kingdom 的国名；不加 the 的有大多数城市、国家、单个山峰。"},{"title":"零冠词——泛指、专有名词与固定搭配","body":"零冠词不是忘记加，而是积极的语法选择！\n\n**泛指复数可数名词或不可数名词：**\n- Dogs are loyal animals.（狗，泛指）\n- Water is essential for life.（水，泛指）\n\n**专有名词：**\n- Beijing, Shakespeare, NASA（一般不加冠词）\n\n**语言/学科/三餐：**\n- She speaks Chinese. / She majors in mathematics.\n- What did you have for breakfast?\n\n**交通方式（by + 交通工具）：**\n- by car, by bus, by plane\n\n**机构功能（强调用途而非建筑）：**\n- go to **school**（上学）vs. go to **the** school（去那所学校）\n- in **prison**（坐牢）vs. in **the** prison（在监狱里）","tip":"三个问题帮你选冠词：①是第一次提到吗？→ a/an 或零冠词；②双方都知道指哪个吗？→ the；③是泛指整个类别吗？→ 零冠词。"},{"title":"中国学生最常犯的冠词错误","body":"**错误1：不可数名词前误加 a/an**\n- ❌ I want to give you an advice.\n- ✅ I want to give you some advice.\n\n**错误2：泛指复数名词前误加 the**\n- ❌ The life is full of challenges.\n- ✅ Life is full of challenges.\n\n**错误3：特指情境漏加 the**\n- ❌ He is best student in our class.\n- ✅ He is **the** best student in our class.\n\n**错误4：固定搭配搞错**\n- ❌ play a piano → ✅ play **the** piano\n- ❌ go to the school（上学）→ ✅ go to **school**\n- ❌ I had a breakfast → ✅ I had **breakfast**\n\n**错误5：专有名词冠词错误**\n- ❌ The China → ✅ China\n- ❌ I visited British Museum → ✅ I visited **the** British Museum","reveal":{"q":"以下哪句话是正确的？\nA. She is a doctor.\nB. She is doctor.\nC. She is the doctor.\n（假设首次介绍身份）","a":"A 正确。介绍职业/身份时用不定冠词 a/an（单数可数名词）。B 漏掉了冠词；C 用 the 暗示特指某位特定的医生，语境不对。"}}],"questions":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"下列哪个词前应该用 an，而不是 a？","options":["a university","an hour","a European","a useful tool"],"answer":1,"explain":"hour 的 h 不发音，发音以元音 /aʊ/ 开头，所以用 an hour。university、European、useful 均以辅音音素 /j/ 开头，用 a。","id":"u2-l1-q1"},{"type":"judge","prompt":"\"advice\" 是可数名词，所以可以说 \"an advice\"。","answer":false,"explain":"advice（建议）是不可数名词，不能加 a/an，也没有复数形式。正确说法是 some advice 或 a piece of advice。","id":"u2-l1-q2"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"填入正确的冠词：\"I saw ___ dog in the park. ___ dog was barking loudly.\"","options":["a, A","a, The","the, The","the, A"],"answer":1,"explain":"第一次提到这只狗，用 a（不定冠词，首次引入）；第二次提到时双方都知道是哪只狗，用 the（定冠词）。","id":"u2-l1-q3"},{"type":"input","prompt":"改正错误：\"She plays ___ piano.\"（填写正确的冠词，演奏乐器）","accept":["the"],"explain":"演奏乐器前用定冠词 the：play the piano, play the violin。注意球类/棋类不加冠词：play chess, play tennis。","id":"u2-l1-q4"},{"type":"judge","prompt":"\"go to school\" 和 \"go to the school\" 意思完全相同。","answer":false,"explain":"go to school 强调上学这一行为/功能（零冠词）；go to the school 指去某所特定的学校建筑（有 the）。含义不同。","id":"u2-l1-q5"},{"type":"match","prompt":"将左边的名词与右边正确的可数性描述配对：","left":["furniture","chair","information","idea"],"right":["可数名词","不可数名词（集合）","可数名词","不可数名词（抽象）"],"explain":"furniture（家具）和 information（信息）是不可数名词；chair（椅子）和 idea（想法）是可数名词。注意 furniture 虽然指很多件东西，但本身是集合不可数名词。","id":"u2-l1-q6"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"下列哪句话的冠词用法是正确的？","options":["The life is short.","She is the best student in our class.","I visited British Museum last week.","He has an knowledge of French."],"answer":1,"explain":"最高级前须用 the，所以 the best student 正确。\"The life\" 错误（泛指用零冠词 life）；\"British Museum\" 缺少 the；\"an knowledge\" 错误（knowledge 不可数，不用 a/an）。","id":"u2-l1-q7"},{"type":"input","prompt":"填空（填入 a、an、the 或 × 表示零冠词）：\"What ___ interesting idea!\"","accept":["an"],"explain":"感叹句 What a/an + 形容词 + 名词！interesting 以元音音素 /ɪ/ 开头，所以用 an。","id":"u2-l1-q8"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"\"She teaches ___ history at ___ university.\"（她在一所大学教历史）正确填空是：","options":["the, a","×, a","the, the","×, the"],"answer":1,"explain":"history 是学科名，泛指时用零冠词；a university 是泛指某一所大学（首次提及，不特指某所），用不定冠词 a。","id":"u2-l1-q9"}]},{"id":"u2-l2","title":"代词与形容词","subtitle":"指代的艺术与描述的精度——从人称代词到形容词比较级","intro":[{"title":"代词的作用：让语言流畅不重复","body":"代词是语言的粘合剂。没有代词，你只能这样说：\n- \"Sarah finished Sarah's project early. Sarah submitted Sarah's project on time.\"\n\n有了代词，就变成：\n- \"Sarah finished **her** project early, and **she** submitted **it** on time.\"\n\n英语代词按功能分为：人称代词、指示代词、不定代词、关系代词、疑问代词。本关逐一讲解。"},{"title":"人称代词：主格、宾格、所有格","body":"英语人称代词根据句子中的角色变化形态：\n\n| 人称 | 主格（作主语） | 宾格（作宾语） | 形容词性所有格 | 名词性所有格 | 反身代词 |\n|------|--------------|--------------|--------------|------------|--------|\n| 第一人称单 | I | me | my | mine | myself |\n| 第二人称 | you | you | your | yours | yourself |\n| 第三人称单(男) | he | him | his | his | himself |\n| 第三人称单(女) | she | her | her | hers | herself |\n| 第三人称单(中) | it | it | its | its | itself |\n| 第一人称复 | we | us | our | ours | ourselves |\n| 第三人称复 | they | them | their | theirs | themselves |\n\n**it's vs. its（最常见拼写错误）：**\n- it's = it is / it has（缩写）：**It's** raining.\n- its = 它的（所有格，无撇号）：The cat licked **its** paw.","tip":"\"Between you and me\"（在你我之间）——介词 between 后必须用宾格 me，不能用 I。\"Between you and I\" 是语法错误！"},{"title":"形容词性所有格 vs. 名词性所有格","body":"两者区别在于：后面有没有名词。\n\n**形容词性所有格（my/your/his/her/its/our/their）——后跟名词：**\n- This is **my** book.（my 修饰 book）\n- That is **her** car.\n\n**名词性所有格（mine/yours/his/hers/its/ours/theirs）——独立使用：**\n- This book is **mine**.（mine = my book）\n- I forgot my umbrella. Can I borrow **yours**?（yours = your umbrella）\n\n**对比：**\n- Your idea is good, but **mine** is better.（mine = my idea，避免重复）"},{"title":"反身代词——什么时候用 myself/yourself...","body":"反身代词有两种用法：\n\n**用法1：动作的接受者就是主语本人（反身用法）**\n- She hurt **herself** while cooking.（她做饭时伤了自己）\n- He taught **himself** to play guitar.（他自学吉他）\n- They enjoyed **themselves** at the party.（他们玩得很开心）\n\n**用法2：强调主语亲自做（可省略不改变句意）**\n- The president **himself** attended.（总统亲自出席）\n- She did it all by **herself**.（她独自完成）\n\n**中国学生常见错误：**\n- ❌ Please contact **myself** if you have questions.\n- ✅ Please contact **me** if you have questions.\n（myself 不能替代 me 作宾语，除非主语是 I）","tip":"口诀：反身代词的主语和宾语必须是同一个人。\"He gave it to John and myself\" 是错的，因为主语是 he，不是 myself 的对应人。"},{"title":"不定代词：some-/any-/no-/every- 系列","body":"16个核心不定代词由词根和后缀组合而成：\n\n| 词根 | -one / -body（人） | -thing（事物） | -where（地点） |\n|------|-------------------|--------------|---------------|\n| some- | someone/somebody | something | somewhere |\n| any- | anyone/anybody | anything | anywhere |\n| no- | no one/nobody | nothing | nowhere |\n| every- | everyone/everybody | everything | everywhere |\n\n**关键区别——some- vs. any-：**\n- **some-**：用于肯定句，或期待肯定回答的疑问句\n  - Someone called you while you were out.\n  - Would you like **something** to eat?（期待对方说要）\n- **any-**：用于否定句、中性疑问句、条件句\n  - I didn't see **anyone** there.\n  - Did **anyone** call?（中性疑问）\n  - You can sit **anywhere** you like.（任意，肯定句也用 any-）\n\n**every- 系列接单数动词：**\n- **Everyone is** here.（不是 are）\n- **Everything is** ready.","tip":"no- 系列相当于 not + any-，所以不能双重否定：Nobody came（✅）= Anybody didn't come（❌）。"},{"title":"关系代词引导定语从句","body":"关系代词（who/whom/whose/which/that）连接主句与定语从句，同时在从句中充当成分。\n\n**区分 who 和 whom：把从句独立成句，看该用 he/she 还是 him/her**\n- The man **who** called you is my uncle. → The man called you. (he) → 用 who\n- The woman **whom** you met is my sister. → You met the woman. (her) → 用 whom\n\n**限制性 vs. 非限制性从句：**\n- 限制性（无逗号，缩小范围，that/who/which 均可）：\n  - The student **that** got the highest score won a prize.\n- 非限制性（有逗号，补充说明，不能用 that）：\n  - My brother, **who** lives in London, is a lawyer.\n  - The Eiffel Tower, **which** was built in 1889, attracts millions.\n\n**which 还可指代整个句子：**\n- He arrived three hours late, **which** annoyed everyone.","tip":"非限制性从句（逗号隔开的）绝对不能用 that！这是考试高频考点。"},{"title":"形容词：比较级与最高级","body":"**规则变化：**\n- 单音节：加 -er/-est → tall → taller → tallest；big → bigger → biggest（双写末辅音）\n- 辅音+y 结尾：y → ier/iest → happy → happier → happiest\n- 多音节（及大多数双音节）：more/most → more beautiful → most beautiful\n\n**不规则变化（必须记忆）：**\n\n| 原级 | 比较级 | 最高级 |\n|------|--------|--------|\n| good/well | better | best |\n| bad/ill | worse | worst |\n| much/many | more | most |\n| little | less | least |\n\n**重要比较句型：**\n- 同级比较：She is **as tall as** her mother.\n- 比较级：Beijing is **larger than** Shanghai.\n- 可数名词用 fewer，不可数用 less：I have **fewer** friends; He has **less** money.\n- 最高级：She is **the tallest** in her class.（in + 群体）\n- 越来越：He is getting **better and better.**\n- 越...越...：**The more** you read, **the better** you write.","tip":"fewer vs. less 是高频易错点：fewer 修饰可数名词（fewer students），less 修饰不可数名词（less water）。"},{"title":"形容词排列顺序 OPSHACOM","body":"多个形容词同时修饰名词时，必须按固定顺序排列：\n\n**顺序：观点 → 大小 → 物理特性 → 形状 → 年龄 → 颜色 → 来源/国籍 → 材料 → 用途**\n\n（记忆口诀：Opinion-Size-Physical-Shape-Age-Color-Origin-Material）\n\n**例子：**\n- a **beautiful tall young Chinese** woman（观点-大小-年龄-来源）\n- a **big round wooden** table（大小-形状-材料）\n- three **small black plastic** buttons（大小-颜色-材料）\n- an **ugly old brown leather** bag（观点-年龄-颜色-材料）\n\n**只能作定语 vs. 只能作表语的特殊形容词：**\n- 只作定语：utter, mere, main, elder, sheer\n  - an utter failure → ❌ The failure is utter.\n- 只作表语：afraid, asleep, alive, alone, awake, aware\n  - She is afraid. → ❌ an afraid girl（应用 frightened）","reveal":{"q":"\"a beautiful small round old Chinese blue ceramic tea\" 这串形容词顺序有问题，正确顺序应该是什么？","a":"正确顺序：a beautiful small round old blue Chinese ceramic tea（观点-大小-形状-年龄-颜色-来源-材料）。颜色(blue)要在来源(Chinese)前面。"}},{"title":"形容词与代词的中式英语陷阱","body":"**陷阱1：形容词作谓语必须加系动词**\n- ❌ This book very interesting. → ✅ This book **is** very interesting.\n\n**陷阱2：只作表语的形容词不能前置**\n- ❌ an afraid girl → ✅ a frightened girl\n- ❌ an asleep baby → ✅ a sleeping baby\n\n**陷阱3：代词格用错**\n- ❌ Between you and **I** → ✅ Between you and **me**（介词后用宾格）\n- ❌ My friend and **myself** went → ✅ My friend and **I** went\n\n**陷阱4：比较级用错**\n- ❌ more better → ✅ better（比较级不加 more）\n- ❌ She is more taller → ✅ She is taller\n- ❌ less students → ✅ **fewer** students（可数名词用 fewer）"}],"questions":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"\"___ is raining, and ___ drops are cold.\"（填写 it's/its 正确选项）","options":["It's, its","Its, it's","It's, it's","Its, its"],"answer":0,"explain":"第一空：it's = it is（天下雨，it 作形式主语，is 缩写为 's）。第二空：its = 它的（雨水的，所有格，无撇号）。","id":"u2-l2-q1"},{"type":"judge","prompt":"\"Please contact myself if you have any questions.\" 这句话语法正确。","answer":false,"explain":"反身代词 myself 只在主语是 I 且动作回指自身时使用。这里主语不是 I，宾语应用普通宾格 me：Please contact me if you have any questions.","id":"u2-l2-q2"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"\"___ did you invite to the party?\"（问被邀请的人，正式书面语）","options":["Who","Whom","Whose","Which"],"answer":1,"explain":"被邀请的人在从句中作动词 invite 的宾语（You invited him/her），宾格用 whom。口语中可用 who，但正式书面语用 whom。","id":"u2-l2-q3"},{"type":"match","prompt":"将左边的形容词与右边它的用法限制配对（选最准确的）：","left":["afraid","main","asleep","utter"],"right":["只能作定语","只能作表语","只能作定语","只能作表语"],"explain":"afraid、asleep 只作表语（不能放名词前，须改用 frightened、sleeping）；main、utter 只作定语（不能放系动词后）。","id":"u2-l2-q4"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"\"She has ___ money than I do, but ___ friends.\"（money 不可数，friends 可数）","options":["less, fewer","fewer, less","less, less","fewer, fewer"],"answer":0,"explain":"money 是不可数名词，用 less；friends 是可数名词，用 fewer。fewer 用于可数，less 用于不可数——这是高频考点。","id":"u2-l2-q5"},{"type":"input","prompt":"用正确的比较级填空：\"The ___ you practice, the ___ you get.\"（much/good 的变化形式）","accept":["more, better","more...better"],"explain":"\"The + 比较级..., the + 比较级\" 句型表示\"越...越...\"。much 的比较级是 more，good 的比较级是 better。","id":"u2-l2-q6"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"下列形容词顺序正确的是：","options":["a Chinese beautiful old silk dress","a beautiful old Chinese silk dress","a silk beautiful Chinese old dress","an old beautiful silk Chinese dress"],"answer":1,"explain":"形容词顺序：观点(beautiful) → 年龄(old) → 来源/国籍(Chinese) → 材料(silk)。所以正确顺序是 a beautiful old Chinese silk dress。","id":"u2-l2-q7"},{"type":"judge","prompt":"非限制性定语从句（逗号隔开的）可以使用关系代词 that。","answer":false,"explain":"非限制性定语从句只能用 who、whom、whose 或 which，不能用 that。例如：My brother, who lives in London, is a lawyer.（不能用 that 替代 who）","id":"u2-l2-q8"},{"type":"input","prompt":"改正错误：\"Everyone are ready to leave.\"（填写正确的动词形式）","accept":["is","Everyone is"],"explain":"every- 系列不定代词（everyone, everybody, everything）在语法上视为单数，接单数动词。正确：Everyone is ready to leave.","id":"u2-l2-q9"}]},{"id":"u2-l3","title":"动词与副词","subtitle":"句子的引擎与调速器——从及物不及物到情态动词与副词位置","intro":[{"title":"动词：句子的核心发动机","body":"动词是句子最重要的词。英语动词按功能分为四大类：\n\n1. **实义动词（Main Verbs）**：有具体意义，分及物（Vt）和不及物（Vi）\n2. **系动词（Linking Verbs）**：连接主语和表语（be, look, feel, become...）\n3. **助动词（Auxiliary Verbs）**：帮助构成时态、语态（be/do/have）\n4. **情态动词（Modals）**：表达情态（can/may/must/will/should...）\n\n本关重点讲解系动词、及物/不及物、情态动词、动名词与不定式、以及副词的用法。"},{"title":"系动词——接形容词，不接副词","body":"系动词连接主语和表语，表语通常是**形容词**（不是副词）。\n\n**判断技巧：把动词换成 be，句意基本不变就是系动词。**\n- She looks tired. → She is tired. ✓（looks 是系动词）\n- She looks at the stars. → She is at the stars. ✗（这里 look 是实义动词）\n\n**常见系动词分类：**\n- **感官类**：look, sound, smell, taste, feel\n  - That sounds **interesting**.（听起来有趣——用形容词，不用副词 interestingly）\n  - The soup tastes **delicious**.\n- **变化类**：become, get, turn, go, grow, fall\n  - It's getting **cold**. / The leaves turned **yellow**. / He fell **asleep**.\n- **保持类**：remain, stay, keep\n  - She remained **calm**. / Keep **quiet**!","tip":"系动词后必须用形容词，不能用副词！错误：She looks beautifully.（❌）→ She looks beautiful.（✅）"},{"title":"及物动词 vs. 不及物动词","body":"**及物动词（Vt）**：动作传递给宾语，需要宾语才能表意完整。\n- She wrote **a letter**.（直接宾语）\n- She gave **him** a book.（间接宾语 him + 直接宾语 a book）\n- 双宾语结构可改写：give a book **to** him；buy flowers **for** her\n\n**不及物动词（Vi）**：动作不传递，不需要宾语。\n- The sun rises. / She smiled. / He arrived late.\n\n**不及物动词常见错误——直接加宾语：**\n- ❌ He arrived the station. → ✅ He arrived **at** the station.\n- ❌ She listened the music. → ✅ She listened **to** the music.\n- ❌ The accident happened us. → ✅ The accident happened **to** us.\n\n**lie vs. lay（中国学生必考点）：**\n- lie（躺，Vi）：lie—lay—lain → Please **lie** down and rest.\n- lay（放置，Vt）：lay—laid—laid → Please **lay** the book on the table.\n- ❌ Please lay down. → ✅ Please lie down.","tip":"to 用于 give/send/tell/show/teach/lend/offer 等；for 用于 buy/make/cook/find/get 等。记住这两组！"},{"title":"情态动词——用语气区分态度","body":"情态动词后接**动词原形**，无第三人称单数 -s，否定/疑问不需要 do。\n\n**能力/许可：can / could**\n- I **can** swim.（我会游泳——能力）\n- **Could** you open the window?（请问能开一下窗吗——礼貌请求，比 can 更正式）\n\n**可能性：may / might**\n- It **may** rain.（可能下雨，约50%）\n- It **might** rain.（或许下雨，约30%，更不确定）\n\n**义务/推断：must / have to**\n- You **must** stop smoking.（必须，内在要求——说话者的命令）\n- I **have to** wear a uniform.（必须，外在规定——公司规定）\n- She's been studying all night—she **must** be exhausted.（一定，强烈推断）\n\n**禁止 vs. 不必要：mustn't vs. don't have to**\n- You **mustn't** enter.（禁止进入）\n- You **don't have to** come.（不必来——不是禁止，是可选的）","tip":"确定性强弱排序（对现在/将来的推测）：must > will > should > may > might/could。He must be home（95%确定）vs. He might be home（30%）。"},{"title":"情态动词进阶：should / would / shall","body":"**should——建议与期望**\n- You **should** see a doctor.（建议，约80%道义确定性）\n- She **should** be here by now.（期望，按理说应该到了）\n- You **should have** told me earlier.（你早该告诉我的——对过去的遗憾）\n\n**would——过去习惯与礼貌**\n- When I was young, I **would** walk to school.（过去经常做的事）\n- **Would** you mind closing the window?（委婉请求，比 will 更礼貌）\n- I **would like** a cup of tea.（= want，礼貌说法）\n\n**shall——提议与正式将来**\n- **Shall** we go?（提议，征求意见）\n- **Shall** I open the door?（我来开门吗？——主动提出帮忙）\n\n**情态动词 + have + 过去分词（对过去推测）：**\n- She **must have** left.（她肯定已经离开了）\n- He **might have** forgotten.（他可能忘了）\n- You **should have** called.（你本该打电话的）\n- She **can't have** done it.（她不可能做了这件事）"},{"title":"动名词 vs. 不定式——接哪个要记清楚","body":"**只接动名词（doing）的常见动词：**\nenjoy, finish, avoid, consider, suggest, practice, admit, deny, mind, quit, keep, give up, put off\n- She **enjoys reading**.（她喜欢读书）\n- He **avoided making** eye contact.\n\n**只接不定式（to do）的常见动词：**\nwant, wish, hope, decide, plan, promise, refuse, agree, manage, fail, afford\n- She **wants to leave**.（她想离开）\n- They **refused to cooperate**.\n\n**两者都可接但意义不同（必考！）：**\n\n| 动词 | + doing | + to do |\n|------|---------|--------|\n| remember | 记得曾经做过（已发生） | 记得要去做（未发生） |\n| forget | 忘记曾经做过 | 忘记去做某事 |\n| stop | 停止做某事（戒掉） | 停下来去做另一件事 |\n| try | 试试看某种方法 | 努力尝试（未必成功） |\n\n- I remember **locking** the door.（我记得我锁了——已锁）\n- Remember **to lock** the door.（记得锁门——提醒）\n- He stopped **smoking**.（他戒烟了）\n- He stopped **to smoke**.（他停下来抽了根烟）","tip":"口诀：stop doing = 停止做这件事；stop to do = 停下手头的事，去做另一件事。两者含义完全不同！"},{"title":"副词的六大类型与位置规则","body":"副词可修饰动词、形容词、其他副词，甚至整个句子。\n\n**六大类型：**\n1. **时间**：yesterday, now, soon, already, yet, just\n2. **地点**：here, there, abroad, upstairs\n3. **方式**：quickly, carefully, well, hard（形副同形）\n4. **程度**：very, extremely, quite, fairly, hardly, almost\n5. **频率**：always（100%）> usually(90%) > often(80%) > sometimes(60%) > rarely(10%) > never(0%)\n6. **语气/句子副词**：Fortunately, Clearly, Honestly, Apparently\n\n**位置规则：**\n- **频率副词** → 句中（be 动词/助动词后；实义动词前）\n  - She **always** gets up at 6. / He has **never** been abroad.\n  - ❌ She reads **often** before bed. → ✅ She **often** reads before bed.\n- **方式副词** → 句末（最自然）\n  - She spoke **softly**.\n- **时间副词** → 句末或句首（不放句中）\n  - ✅ She called **yesterday**. / ✅ **Yesterday** she called.\n  - ❌ She **yesterday** called.\n- **程度副词** → 紧靠被修饰词前\n  - She is **very** happy. / He **almost** missed the bus.","tip":"only/even 的位置影响语义！Only she called me（只有她）vs. She only called me（只是打电话）vs. She called only me（只给我打）——位置不同，意思完全不同！"},{"title":"易混淆：形容词与副词同根对","body":"加 -ly 后意义可能大变！\n\n| 形容词/副词 | 加 -ly 后 | 含义对比 |\n|------------|----------|--------|\n| hard（努力的/努力地） | hardly（几乎不） | She works **hard**. / I **hardly** know him. |\n| late（晚的/晚地） | lately（最近） | He arrived **late**. / **Lately** I've been tired. |\n| near（近的/近地） | nearly（几乎） | We live **near** the park. / I **nearly** forgot. |\n| high（高地） | highly（高度地/非常） | The bird flew **high**. / She is **highly** respected. |\n| deep（深地，物理） | deeply（深深地，情感） | Dig **deep**. / She was **deeply** moved. |\n| close（近地） | closely（仔细地/密切地） | Sit **close** to me. / Watch **closely**. |\n\n**最常见易错：**\n- ❌ He **hard** ate anything. → ✅ He **hardly** ate anything.（几乎没吃）\n- ❌ Have you seen her **near**ly? → ✅ Have you seen her **lately**?（最近）","reveal":{"q":"\"You don't have to come\" 和 \"You mustn't come\" 有什么区别？","a":"don't have to = 不必，是可选的，没有强制性；mustn't = 禁止，绝对不能来。两者意义完全相反！这是英语情态动词的高频考点。"}}],"questions":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"\"She looks ___. \"（她看起来很累）正确填入：","options":["tiredly","tired","tire","tiring"],"answer":1,"explain":"look 是系动词，后面接形容词（表语），不接副词。tired（累的，形容词）是正确答案。tiring 意为\"令人疲倦的\"，意思不对。","id":"u2-l3-q1"},{"type":"judge","prompt":"\"He arrived the station at noon.\" 这句话语法正确。","answer":false,"explain":"arrive 是不及物动词，不能直接跟宾语，需要加介词 at：He arrived at the station at noon. 类似的还有 listen to, happen to 等。","id":"u2-l3-q2"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"\"You ___ come if you're busy—it's optional.\"（不必来，可选的）","options":["mustn't","don't have to","can't","shouldn't"],"answer":1,"explain":"don't have to = 不必，是可选的，没有强制性。mustn't = 禁止（绝对不可以来）。这两者意义完全相反，是高频考点。","id":"u2-l3-q3"},{"type":"match","prompt":"将左边的句子与右边的含义配对：","left":["I remember locking the door.","Remember to lock the door.","He stopped smoking.","He stopped to smoke."],"right":["停下手头的事，去抽烟","记得（去）锁门——提醒","戒烟了","记得（曾经）锁了门"],"explain":"remember doing = 记得曾经做过（已发生）；remember to do = 记得要去做（未发生）。stop doing = 停止做该事；stop to do = 停下来去做另一件事。","id":"u2-l3-q4"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"下列句子中频率副词位置正确的是：","options":["She reads often before bed.","She often reads before bed.","Often she reads before bed.","She reads before bed often."],"answer":1,"explain":"频率副词（often）放在实义动词（reads）前面。句首（Often she reads...）语法上也可接受，但不是最自然的位置。放在句末（reads before bed often）通常不自然。","id":"u2-l3-q5"},{"type":"input","prompt":"填空：\"I ___ know him.\"（我几乎不认识他，填入一个副词）","accept":["hardly","scarcely","barely"],"explain":"hardly = 几乎不，是正确答案。注意 hard 是「努力地」，意义完全不同。hardly、scarcely、barely 都表示「几乎不」。","id":"u2-l3-q6"},{"type":"judge","prompt":"\"She must be exhausted.\" 这里 must 表示强制义务（必须做某事）。","answer":false,"explain":"这里 must 表示强烈推断（她肯定精疲力竭了）。must 有两个核心用法：①强制义务（You must stop.）；②强烈推断/逻辑判断（She must be tired.）。语境判断：be exhausted 描述状态，是推断用法。","id":"u2-l3-q7"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"\"The bird flew ___.\"（鸟飞得很高，物理高度）和 \"She is ___ respected.\"（她备受尊重）分别应填：","options":["high, high","highly, highly","high, highly","highly, high"],"answer":2,"explain":"fly high = 飞得高（物理高度，同形副词）；highly respected = 备受尊重（程度副词，修饰形容词/分词时用 highly）。high 和 highly 含义不同：high 指物理高度，highly 指程度「非常地/高度地」。","id":"u2-l3-q8"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"下列哪个句子中的情态动词用法正确？","options":["She cans speak three languages.","You should have told me earlier.","He might to arrive tomorrow.","They must to follow the rules."],"answer":1,"explain":"情态动词后接动词原形（不加 to），且无第三人称单数 -s。cans（❌），might to arrive（❌），must to follow（❌）都错误。\"should have told\" = 对过去的遗憾，格式正确（情态动词 + have + 过去分词）。","id":"u2-l3-q9"}]},{"id":"u2-l4","title":"介词、连词与感叹词","subtitle":"关系、连接与情感的语言编码——从 at/on/in 到 FANBOYS 与从属连词","intro":[{"title":"介词：认知地图，不是死记硬背","body":"介词让中国学生头疼，是因为很多人把介词当孤立搭配死背。其实介词有规律：**所有抽象用法都源于基本的空间含义**。\n\n**空间 → 时间 → 抽象（依次扩展）：**\n\n- **in**（在里面）：in the room（空间）→ in 2024（时间段）→ in trouble/in love（抽象状态）\n- **on**（在表面接触）：on the table（空间）→ on Monday（特定日期）→ on sale/on duty（运作状态）\n- **at**（在某个点）：at the door（空间点）→ at noon（时刻点）→ at risk/at war（状态节点）\n\n理解这个规律，就能从「理解」而非「背诵」出发，举一反三。"},{"title":"时间介词：at/on/in 三层结构","body":"时间介词是使用频率最高、最容易出错的类别：\n\n**AT（点）→ 精确时刻：**\n- at 6 o'clock / at noon / at midnight / at dawn\n- at the weekend（英式）/ at Christmas\n- at night（晚上，不是 in the night）\n- at the age of 6（在6岁时）\n\n**ON（面）→ 具体日期/特定某天：**\n- on Monday / on weekdays / on weekends（美式）\n- on March 15th / on my birthday / on New Year's Day\n- on time（准时，按计划）vs. in time（及时，来得及）\n\n**IN（段）→ 较长时间段：**\n- in the morning / in January / in summer / in 2024\n- in the 21st century\n- in time（及时）vs. on time（准时）\n- in the end（最终）vs. at the end（在结尾处）","tip":"on time vs. in time：on time = 准点，按时间表；in time = 及时，没有错过。\"The train arrived on time.\"（火车准点到）vs. \"I arrived just in time.\"（我刚好赶上了）"},{"title":"易混淆时间介词：by/until、since/for、in/within","body":"**by vs. until（till）：**\n- **by**（截止，强调「不迟于某时」，一次性动作）\n  - Please finish this **by** Friday.（周五前完成）\n  - She will be back **by** 6 pm.\n- **until/till**（持续直到某时间点）\n  - I waited **until** midnight.（我等到午夜）\n  - Don't leave **until** I come back.\n- 对比：I'll work **by** Friday.（周五前完成——结果）vs. I'll work **until** Friday.（工作到周五——过程）\n\n**since vs. for：**\n- **since** + 时间点（从某个时间点开始，用完成时）\n  - She has lived here **since** 2010.\n- **for** + 时间段（持续了多长时间）\n  - She has lived here **for** ten years.\n\n**in vs. within：**\n- **in** ten minutes = 从现在起10分钟后\n- **within** 24 hours = 在24小时之内（强调不超过）","tip":"since 后接时间点（since 2010 / since Monday）；for 后接时间段（for ten years / for three days）。这是完成时考题的核心考点！"},{"title":"地点介词：above/over、below/under、between/among","body":"**above vs. over（上方）：**\n- **above**：高于某物，不一定正上方，不涉及覆盖\n  - The plane flew **above** the clouds.（飞机在云层上方飞行）\n  - Her score is **above** average.（成绩在平均分以上）\n- **over**：直接在正上方，或「覆盖」，或「越过」，或「超过」\n  - There's a lamp **over** the table.（灯在桌子正上方）\n  - She spread a blanket **over** the bed.（盖上毯子）\n  - **over** 100 people = more than 100 people\n\n**below vs. under（下方）：**\n- **below**：低于某物（不一定正下方），抽象场景多\n  - The temperature fell **below** freezing.\n- **under**：直接在正下方，或覆盖之下，抽象含义丰富\n  - The cat is **under** the table.\n  - **under** pressure / **under** control / **under** construction\n\n**between vs. among：**\n- **between**：两个独立个体之间（也可用于三个明确个体之间）\n  - She sat **between** Tom and Mary.\n- **among**：三者或多者组成的群体内部\n  - She is the most talented **among** her classmates.\n\n**beside vs. besides：**\n- **beside**（介词）：在...旁边（空间）\n- **besides**（介词/副词）：除了...之外（还）\n  - **Besides** English, she speaks French.（除了英语，她还会法语）"},{"title":"并列连词 FANBOYS——连接对等成分","body":"英语并列连词共 7 个，用首字母组成 **FANBOYS**：\n\n| 连词 | 含义 | 例句 |\n|------|------|------|\n| **F**or | 因为（正式） | He must be tired, **for** he's worked all day. |\n| **A**nd | 和，然后 | She is intelligent **and** hardworking. |\n| **N**or | 也不 | She doesn't smoke, **nor** does she drink. |\n| **B**ut | 但是 | It was expensive **but** worth it. |\n| **O**r | 或者，否则 | Hurry up, **or** you'll miss the train. |\n| **Y**et | 然而（语气强） | She is young, **yet** very mature. |\n| **S**o | 所以 | It was raining, **so** we stayed inside. |\n\n**标点规则：**\n- 连接两个独立句子：**逗号 + 连词**\n  - ✅ She was tired, **but** she kept working.\n  - ❌ She was tired, she kept working.（逗号拼接错误 Comma Splice，严重语法错误！）\n- 连接单词/短语：不加逗号（tea and coffee）","tip":"nor 后面要倒装！\"She doesn't smoke, nor does she drink.\"（不能说 nor she drinks）"},{"title":"从属连词——时间、原因、条件、让步","body":"从属连词引导的从句依附于主句，语义关系丰富：\n\n**时间连词（when/while/as/until/as soon as）：**\n- **while**（同时进行两个动作）：While he was cooking, she was reading.\n- **until**（直到...才）：Wait here **until** I return.\n- **as soon as**（一...就...）：**As soon as** she heard the news, she called.\n\n**原因连词（because/since/as）：**\n- **because**（最直接，可放句首或句中）：She was late **because** her car broke down.\n- **since/as**（原因已知，语气弱，通常句首）：**Since** you're here, you might as well help.\n\n**条件连词（if/unless/as long as/in case）：**\n- **unless** = if...not：**Unless** you hurry, you'll be late.\n- **as long as**（只要）：**As long as** you try your best, I'll be proud.\n- **in case**（以防，预防性）：Take an umbrella **in case** it rains.（不是 if it rains）\n\n**让步连词（although/though/even though/even if）：**\n- **even though** > **although** > **though**（语气由强到弱）\n- **even if**（即使，假设性）：**Even if** I fail, I won't give up.\n- ❌ Despite he was tired... → ✅ Although he was tired...（despite/in spite of 后接名词，不接从句！）","tip":"in case ≠ if！in case 强调「提前预防」：Take an umbrella in case it rains.（带伞以防下雨）。if 表示条件：Take an umbrella if it rains.（下雨的话带伞）。两者时态和含义都不同。"},{"title":"关联连词——成对出现，要求平行结构","body":"关联连词成对使用，**连接的两部分必须结构平行**（都是名词、都是形容词、都是句子等）。\n\n**both...and（两者都）：**\n- She is both **intelligent** and **hardworking**.（两个形容词，平行）\n- ❌ She is both intelligent and **works hard**.（形容词 vs. 动词短语，不平行）\n\n**either...or（要么...要么，两选一）：**\n- Either you come with me, or you stay here.\n- 动词就近一致：**Either** he or his brothers **are** responsible.（brothers 靠近动词）\n\n**neither...nor（既不...也不）：**\n- She speaks **neither** French **nor** German.\n\n**not only...but also（不仅...而且）：**\n- She is **not only** talented **but also** dedicated.\n- ⚠️ Not only 位于句首时，**主句须倒装**：\n  - ✅ **Not only did** he apologize, but he also offered to help.\n  - ❌ Not only he apologized, but he also helped.\n\n**目的结果连词：**\n- **so...that**（如此...以至于）：He was **so** tired **that** he fell asleep.\n- **such...that**（如此...以至于，接名词短语）：It was **such** a good film **that** we watched it twice.","reveal":{"q":"\"Despite she was tired, she kept smiling.\" 这句话对吗？如何改正？","a":"错误。despite 和 in spite of 是介词，后接名词或动名词，不能接从句（that/she/he 等）。改法：①Although she was tired, she kept smiling.（用从属连词 although）；②Despite her tiredness, she kept smiling.（用名词）；③In spite of being tired, she kept smiling.（用动名词）"}},{"title":"感叹词与话语标记——地道英语的润滑剂","body":"**感叹词（Interjections）——表达情感，独立使用：**\n- 惊讶：Oh! / Wow! / Gosh! / Good heavens!\n- 高兴：Great! / Fantastic! / Yay! / Hooray!\n- 痛苦：Ouch! / Ow!（疼痛）/ Oh no!（失望）\n- 犹豫：Um... / Uh... / Hmm... / Er...\n\n**话语标记（Discourse Markers）——组织对话，表达态度：**\n\n| 功能 | 常用词 |\n|------|--------|\n| 顺序 | First / Then / Finally |\n| 增加信息 | Also / Furthermore / Moreover / In addition |\n| 转折 | However / Nevertheless / On the other hand |\n| 举例 | For example / For instance / Such as |\n| 总结 | In conclusion / To sum up / In short |\n| 诚实表态 | Honestly / Frankly / To be honest |\n| 显然 | Obviously / Clearly / Apparently |\n| 软化语气 | I think / I believe / It seems / Perhaps |\n\n⚠️ 口语中过度使用 \"like\"、\"you know\" 是不成熟的标志，正式表达中要尽量避免。"},{"title":"词性转换规律——掌握词根，词汇翻倍","body":"英语通过前缀和后缀进行词性转换，掌握规律可以大幅扩展词汇量。\n\n**动词 → 名词：**\n- -tion/-sion：create → **creation**, decide → **decision**\n- -ment：develop → **development**, achieve → **achievement**\n- -ance/-ence：perform → **performance**, prefer → **preference**\n- -er/-or：teach → **teacher**, act → **actor**\n\n**名词/动词 → 形容词：**\n- -ful/-less：hope → **hopeful / hopeless**\n- -ous/-ious：danger → **dangerous**, glory → **glorious**\n- -able/-ible：read → **readable**, sense → **sensible**\n- -ing（主动）/ -ed（被动）：interest → **interesting** book / **interested** student\n\n**形容词 → 副词（通常 + -ly）：**\n- quick → **quickly**, happy → **happily**, dramatic → **dramatically**\n\n**词族示例：**\n- educate(V) → education(N) → educational(Adj) → educationally(Adv) → educator(N)\n- create(V) → creation(N) → creative(Adj) → creatively(Adv) → creativity(N)"}],"questions":[{"type":"choice","prompt":"\"She has been working here ___ 2019.\"（从2019年起）和 \"She has been working here ___ five years.\"（持续了五年）正确填入：","options":["since, for","for, since","since, since","for, for"],"answer":0,"explain":"since 后接时间点（since 2019），for 后接时间段（for five years）。这是完成时的核心搭配。","id":"u2-l4-q1"},{"type":"judge","prompt":"\"Please finish this report until Friday.\"（意在表达：周五之前完成）这句话是正确的。","answer":false,"explain":"by 表示「截止，不迟于某时」（一次性动作结束）；until 表示「持续直到」。这里应该用 by：Please finish this report by Friday.（周五前完成这份报告）","id":"u2-l4-q2"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"\"She is talented ___ also very dedicated.\"（不仅...而且...，not only 在句首时）","options":["Not only she is, but","Not only is she, but","Not only she, but","Not only does she, but"],"answer":1,"explain":"Not only 位于句首时，后面的从句须倒装（助动词提前）。She is talented → Not only is she talented, but also very dedicated. 注意是 is she，不是 she is。","id":"u2-l4-q3"},{"type":"match","prompt":"将左边的情况与右边应该用 above 还是 over 配对：","left":["灯在桌子正上方","她的成绩在平均分以上","她把毯子盖在床上","超过100人参加"],"right":["above（高于，抽象比较）","over（正上方，接触/覆盖）","over（超过数量）","over（正上方）"],"explain":"above 表示「高于某物」，用于抽象比较（above average）或飞机飞在云层上方（不直接接触）；over 表示「正上方」（a lamp over the table）、「覆盖」（spread a blanket over）或「超过数量」（over 100 people）。","id":"u2-l4-q4"},{"type":"judge","prompt":"\"Despite he was tired, he kept working.\" 语法正确。","answer":false,"explain":"despite 和 in spite of 是介词，后面只能接名词或动名词，不能接句子（不能接 he/she/that 等引导的从句）。正确改法：Although he was tired, he kept working.（用连词）或 Despite his tiredness, he kept working.（用名词）","id":"u2-l4-q5"},{"type":"input","prompt":"填入正确的介词：\"Take an umbrella ___ it rains.\"（提前预防，不是条件）","accept":["in case"],"explain":"in case 表示「以防」，强调提前预防。if 表示「如果」，是条件关系。Take an umbrella in case it rains（带伞以防万一下雨）表达的是预防，而非等下雨了才带伞。","id":"u2-l4-q6"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"\"She is both intelligent ___ works very hard.\" 这句话：","options":["正确，and 后面可以跟动词短语","错误，both...and 要求平行结构，应改为 both intelligent and hardworking","错误，应该用 not only...but also","正确，口语中可以接受"],"answer":1,"explain":"both...and 要求严格的平行结构：both A and B 中，A 和 B 必须是相同的语法成分。intelligent 是形容词，works very hard 是动词短语，不平行。正确：She is both intelligent and hardworking.（两个形容词）","id":"u2-l4-q7"},{"type":"choice","prompt":"\"___ you and me, this plan won't work.\"（私下里，between 还是 among？）","options":["Between","Among","Beside","Besides"],"answer":0,"explain":"between 用于两个独立个体之间（you and me = 两个人）；among 用于三者或多者组成的群体内部。\"between you and me\" 是固定短语，意为「私下里，我们之间」。","id":"u2-l4-q8"},{"type":"judge","prompt":"并列连词连接两个完整句子时，可以只用逗号而不用连词，如：\"She was tired, she kept working.\"","answer":false,"explain":"这是「逗号拼接错误」（Comma Splice），是英语写作中的严重语法错误。两个独立句子必须用并列连词连接（逗号 + but/and/so 等）：She was tired, but she kept working. 或用分号：She was tired; she kept working.","id":"u2-l4-q9"}]}]}